```sql
--Description:  Return a compact view of repositories that **actually**
--              declare a recognised feature‑toggle library.  We begin with
--              `repository_dependencies` (rd) and filter rows where the
--              dependency name contains any of the strings we have already
--              seen in the data: “launchdarkly”, “ldclient” (JS/Node SDKs),
--              “flipper”, “featuretoggle” (or “feature‑toggles”), and
--              “django‑waffle”.  We then LEFT JOIN to `repositories` (r)
--              using the textual keys (`name_with_owner`, `host_type`) so
--              we still retrieve repository details even when `repository_id`
--              is NULL.  A second LEFT JOIN to `projects` (p) adds canonical
--              library information (name & languages).  The query selects
