Successfully corrected. SQL:
--Description:  Determine the leading programming languages among
--              repositories that use a feature‑toggle library.  Approach:
--              1.  Filter `repository_dependencies` (rd) to rows whose
--                  dependency name (lower‑cased) contains any of the
--                  substrings that clearly point to a feature‑toggle
--                  solution:  “launchdarkly”, “ldclient”, “flipper”,
--                  “featuretoggle” / “feature‑toggles”, or “django‑waffle”.
--                  Using %substr% LIKE makes the filter resilient to
--                  suffixes/prefixes (e.g. “flipper-plugin”, “ldclient-js”).
--              2.  LEFT JOIN to `repositories` (r) on the textual key
--                  `name_with_owner` only.  Dropping `host_type` from the
--                  join ensures we still bring in repository rows even when
--                  host_type differs or the repository entry is partially
--                  missing (the earlier exact‑key joins yielded zero rows).
--              3.  Use COALESCE so that repos without a detected language
--                  are bucketed under the label 'Unknown'.
--              4.  Aggregate distinct repositories per language and sort by
--                  descending count.  LIMIT 20 gives the most frequent
--                  languages for inspection.
SELECT
       COALESCE(r.language, 'Unknown') AS language,
       COUNT(DISTINCT rd.repository_name_with_owner) AS repo_count
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.libraries_io.repository_dependencies` rd
LEFT  JOIN `bigquery-public-data.libraries_io.repositories`        r
       ON  r.name_with_owner = rd.repository_name_with_owner
WHERE  LOWER(rd.dependency_project_name) LIKE '%launchdarkly%'
   OR  LOWER(rd.dependency_project_name) LIKE '%ldclient%'
   OR  LOWER(rd.dependency_project_name) LIKE '%flipper%'
   OR  LOWER(rd.dependency_project_name) LIKE '%featuretoggle%'
   OR  LOWER(rd.dependency_project_name) LIKE '%feature-toggles%'
   OR  LOWER(rd.dependency_project_name) LIKE '%django-waffle%'
GROUP BY language
ORDER BY repo_count DESC
LIMIT 20;
