--------------------------------------------------
Table full name: bigquery-public-data.libraries_io.repository_dependencies
Column name: id Type: INT64 Description: The unique primary key of the repository dependency in the Libraries.io database.
Column name: host_type Type: STRING Description: Which website the dependencys repository is hosted on, either GitHub, GitLab or Bitbucket.
Column name: repository_name_with_owner Type: STRING Description: The repository name and owner seperated by a slash, also maps to the url slug on the given repository host e.g. librariesio/libraries.io.
Column name: repository_id Type: INT64 Description: The unique primary key of the repository for this dependency in the Libraries.io database.
Column name: manifest_platform Type: STRING Description: Which package manager the dependency listed in the manifest should use.
Column name: manifest_filepath Type: STRING Description: Path to the file where the dependency is declared within the repository.
Column name: git_branch Type: STRING Description: Which branch was the manifest loaded from the repository.
Column name: manifest_kind Type: STRING Description: Either manifest or lockfile, manifests are written by humans, lockfiles contain full resolved dependency tree.
Column name: optional Type: STRING Description: Is the dependency optional?.
Column name: dependency_project_name Type: STRING Description: The name of the project that the dependency specifies.
Column name: dependency_requirements Type: STRING Description: The version or range of versions that the dependency specifies, resolution of that to a particular version is package manager specific.
Column name: dependency_kind Type: STRING Description: The type of dependency, often declared for the phase of usage, e.g. runtime, test, development, build.
Column name: dependency_project_id Type: INT64 Description: The unique primary key of the project for this dependency in the Libraries.io database.
